{
    // Standard SigmaFi V2 bond vault. No off-chain code exists yet.
    // Receives every ZC_Standard_Bond settlement. One vault serves every bond: it has no constants.
    // The holder of the circulating bond unit claims the whole box by burning all 3 units.
    //
    // TOKENS
    // tokens(0): (bond asset, 2) - the reserve the bond carried here. Because supply is exactly 3,
    //   this is the only box that can hold 2 units: it is found by token id and it authenticates
    //   itself, off-chain and as a data input. A fake vault naming the asset cannot hold the reserve.
    // tokens(1..): settlement proceeds
    //
    // REGISTERS (enforced by the bond, not read here)
    // R4: Coll[Byte] - id of the bond box this settles
    // R5: Byte - settlement path: 0 repaid, 1 liquidated
    //
    // SPENDING
    // More of the asset than this box's reserve must be spent, and none may survive: the circulating
    // unit is presented and all 3 units are burned. Outputs are otherwise unconstrained, so a holder
    // may sweep any number of settled bonds in one transaction, and a consuming contract such as
    // ZC_Standard_FractionalVault can direct the proceeds into itself.
    //
    // ASSUMPTIONS
    // - The asset came from a verified ZC_Standard_Order mint: supply 3, reserve 2. For any other token the
    //   rule still only releases a box to someone who burns more of tokens(0) than the box holds.
    // - Value sent here outside a bond settlement is a gift to that asset's holder.
    // - A lost circulating unit strands the proceeds. No timeout or sweep authority exists.
    // - Storage-rent collection is outside script evaluation and is not modelled.

    def numTokenInOutputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        OUTPUTS.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) =>
            val count = b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                if (t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
            })
            a + count
        })
    }

    def numTokenInInputs(tokenId: Coll[Byte]): Long = {
        INPUTS.fold(0L, { (a: Long, b: Box) =>
            val count = b.tokens.fold(0L, { (z: Long, t: (Coll[Byte], Long)) =>
                if (t._1 == tokenId) z + t._2 else z
            })
            a + count
        })
    }

    val asset = SELF.tokens(0)._1
    val reserve = SELF.tokens(0)._2
    sigmaProp(numTokenInInputs(asset) > reserve && numTokenInOutputs(asset) == 0L)
}
